WEBVTT

1
00:00:08.534 --> 00:00:11.692
Norbert Weiner was a famous professor.

2
00:00:11.693 --> 00:00:14.282
He was a very intelligent man.

3
00:00:14.283 --> 00:00:19.996
However, he was very forgetful.

4
00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:24.620
One day, the Weiner family was moving to another house.

5
00:00:24.621 --> 00:00:29.034
Mrs. Weiner knew that her husband wouldn't be much help moving.

6
00:00:29.035 --> 00:00:36.159
So she sent him to school while she and the movers worked together.

7
00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:42.113
Mrs. Weiner was sure that Professor Weiner would forget that they had moved.

8
00:00:42.114 --> 00:00:46.104
She wrote down their new address on a piece of paper.

9
00:00:46.105 --> 00:00:55.020
She gave it to him and said, "Honey, this is our new address. Don't forget!"

10
00:00:55.021 --> 00:01:01.743
"All right, darling," replied Professor Weiner as he kissed his wife good-bye.

11
00:01:01.744 --> 00:01:08.441
"Good-bye, and have a nice day at school," said Mrs. Weiner.

12
00:01:08.442 --> 00:01:12.908
While at school, Professor Weiner had a great idea.

13
00:01:12.909 --> 00:01:17.389
He decided to write it down in case he forgot it.

14
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:24.106
He reached into his pocket and took out a piece of paper.

15
00:01:24.107 --> 00:01:27.195
He wrote his idea down with a pencil.

16
00:01:27.196 --> 00:01:34.475
But of course, it was the piece of paper with his new address on it!

17
00:01:34.476 --> 00:01:39.161
Later, Professor Weiner looked at the piece of paper again.

18
00:01:39.162 --> 00:01:41.335
He read his idea.

19
00:01:41.336 --> 00:01:45.887
He decided it wasn't very good and threw the paper away.

20
00:01:45.888 --> 00:01:53.459
And yes, it was the piece of paper with the new address on it!

21
00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.278
At the end of the day, he left for home.

22
00:01:57.279 --> 00:01:59.738
He went to his old address.

23
00:01:59.739 --> 00:02:05.205
He completely forgot that his family had moved.

24
00:02:05.206 --> 00:02:08.110
When he got there, the house was empty.

25
00:02:08.111 --> 00:02:11.755
He thought about the piece of paper from that morning.

26
00:02:11.756 --> 00:02:14.352
He remembered that he threw it away.

27
00:02:14.353 --> 00:02:18.599
But he couldn't remember the address that was written on it.

28
00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:23.801
He thought and thought about what to do.

29
00:02:23.802 --> 00:02:27.665
The sun had set and he was very worried.

30
00:02:27.666 --> 00:02:33.721
Fortunately, he noticed a young girl playing behind the house.

31
00:02:33.722 --> 00:02:37.648
He walked over to the girl in the darkness and said,

32
00:02:37.649 --> 00:02:42.639
"Excuse me, I'm Norbert Weiner and my family has just moved.

33
00:02:42.640 --> 00:02:46.725
Maybe you know where we've moved to?"

34
00:02:46.726 --> 00:02:53.397
The young girl replied, "Yes, Daddy. Mommy knew you would forget.

35
00:02:53.398 --> 00:02:58.451
I'll take you home now."
